Description: plasma: Keep Xlib's names out of the depth exchange
 .
 libstereo-declare's header includes Xlib for its X11 calls, and Xlib defines
 Expose, None, Bool, Status and Unsorted as macros, which broke QEvent::Expose
 in the Plasma platform built against the real library 1.5 rather than a
 stand-in.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: https://invent.kde.org/danielcamposramos/union/-/commit/43ef0b44894c74f70e1f095081a1113238b04be3
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-23
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 src/platform/plasma/PlasmaDepthExchange.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/platform/plasma/PlasmaDepthExchange.cpp b/src/platform/plasma/PlasmaDepthExchange.cpp
index 536910f4..120469bb 100644
--- a/src/platform/plasma/PlasmaDepthExchange.cpp
+++ b/src/platform/plasma/PlasmaDepthExchange.cpp
@@ -11,6 +11,12 @@
 #include <qpa/qplatformnativeinterface.h>
 
 #include <stereo-declare.h>
+// The library's header includes Xlib for its X11 calls, and Xlib defines names Qt uses.
+#undef Expose
+#undef None
+#undef Bool
+#undef Status
+#undef Unsorted
 
 PlasmaDepthExchange::PlasmaDepthExchange(std::function<void(QWindow *)> changed, QObject *parent)
     : QObject(parent)
